invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: rsa_sign64_sp1 returns without wiping the candidate's bytes.
  After a check that passed they are the signature the caller holds. A
  candidate that failed its check differs from the signature modulo one
  prime alone, and it and the message factor the modulus.
  bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test signs under a key with one bit of dp changed,
  copies the stack below the refused call and finds the candidate's bytes
  there.

--- old
    ct_wipe(s, sizeof s);
    ct_wipe(candidate, sizeof candidate);
--- new
    ct_wipe(s, sizeof s);
